---
title: "Drawbridge — Review state machine: the system refuses to guess"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  direction TB
  [*] --> INTAKE

  INTAKE --> QUESTIONNAIRE_OUT : plan checkpointed
  QUESTIONNAIRE_OUT --> GATED : P1 · no approval token for first contact
  GATED --> QUESTIONNAIRE_OUT : contact authorised, single-use token spent
  QUESTIONNAIRE_OUT --> REPLIES_IN : coverage reaches 90 percent
  REPLIES_IN --> EVIDENCE_REVIEW : documents screened and stamped
  EVIDENCE_REVIEW --> SCORED : findings reconciled
  SCORED --> GATED : G1 · memo written, waiting on a named human
  GATED --> DECIDED : signed approval token, identity recorded
  DECIDED --> MONITORED : watchdog takes over the vendor
  MONITORED --> MONITORED : scheduled sweep, no signal

  MONITORED --> EVIDENCE_REVIEW : watchdog.hit opens a NEW linked review

  INTAKE --> NEEDS_HUMAN
  QUESTIONNAIRE_OUT --> NEEDS_HUMAN : three chases, no reply
  REPLIES_IN --> NEEDS_HUMAN : answer below the confidence threshold
  EVIDENCE_REVIEW --> NEEDS_HUMAN : corrupt or unreadable document
  SCORED --> NEEDS_HUMAN : invalid transition or DLQ exhaustion

  NEEDS_HUMAN --> [*] : analyst resolves and the review resumes

  note right of GATED
    One state, two scopes.
    gate_scope = contact  → P1, first outbound email
    gate_scope = decision → G1, risk acceptance
    Both are signed, single-use and scoped,
    and both are enforced at the gateway —
    never in the user interface.
  end note

  note right of NEEDS_HUMAN
    Enterable from any state.
    Parks the review with a dashboard card
    explaining what stalled and why.
    It never silently corrects.
  end note

  note left of MONITORED
    History is never mutated.
    A reopened review is a new record
    linked to the old one, so the
    audit trail stays intact.
  end note
